abstract: >-
  nealab is a reproducible platform for subnational territorial
  analysis. It combines satellite imagery (Sentinel-1/2, MODIS, Landsat),
  census data, and open geospatial datasets into PCA-validated composite
  indicators on a hexagonal grid (H3 resolution 9). The pipeline runs on
  Google Earth Engine, processes rasters into H3 zonal statistics, computes
  scores using geometric means validated by KMO/Bartlett/PCA diagnostics
  (OECD Handbook / UNDP HDI methodology), and serves results via DuckDB-WASM
  on Cloudflare Pages. Applied to 24 subnational territories across the NEA
  (northeast Argentina) and its cross-border regions (Paraguay, southern
  Brazil), ranging from ~320,000 hexagons for Misiones to ~1.1 million for
  Chaco, with 16 hexagon-level analyses and 8 census-tract-level analyses
  across four thematic lenses: investment, production, services, and housing.
